The sets satisfying (i) and (ii) form the *induced topology* on a partially ordered set $X$, which is still a $T_0$-space because the sets $\{ x \in X : x \not\sqsubseteq y \}$ remain open even in the sense of (ii). Obviously a directed set $S \subseteq X$ can be regarded as a net, and now in view of (ii) it follows that $S$ converges to $\bigsqcup S$ — if this lub exists.
